findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config_loading tests don't test distinguishing NotFound from parse/permission
    errors, and the reviewer didn't flag this specific silent error swallowing pattern.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented CWE-209 safe Display impls in error.rs \u2014 ServerError\
    \ shows 'server error \u2014 contact your administrator' without leaking internals.\
    \ Reviewer verified: '[VERIFIED] CWE-209 error Display messages do not leak internals.'\
    \ However, this applies to Display impl, not to the eprintln!() call site which\
    \ still prints Display directly to stderr. Partially caught \u2014 the Display\
    \ is sanitized but the stderr leakage pattern itself was not flagged."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests for CRLF in tenant IDs, but the reviewer\
    \ flagged these as vacuous (tests pass for wrong reason). The actual issue \u2014\
    \ using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 was not identified\
    \ by any phase. The reviewer flagged silent header drops but not the type-safety\
    \ gap of using String vs TenantId."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer noted toml version mismatch but not the workspace
    dependency pattern violation.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: ''ClientConfig silently accepts unknown fields
    including token... #[serde(default)] without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] means
    a config file containing token = "my-secret" is silently accepted and ignored...
    Should either deny unknown fields or at minimum warn.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...). The TEA wrote config tests but this specific logical flaw in the assertion
    was not caught.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the test with zero assertions (let _ = config). TEA
    wrote 11 config tests but didn't flag or fix this vacuous test pattern.
